{"custom_id":"s-ap_microeconomics-m02-k3","ok":true,"model":"claude-opus-5-5","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgGCJYHbLGKvpVnbQdsxw","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Whichever side of the market is less elastic carries more of a tax. Here supply (elasticity 0.5) is less elastic than demand (absolute elasticity 3.0), so producers bear the larger share.\n\nUsing the standard approximation, the consumers' share is Es/(Es+|Ed|) = 0.5/3.5 ≈ 14%. The producers' share is |Ed|/(Es+|Ed|) = 3.0/3.5 ≈ 86%.\n\nThis makes E (index 4) the correct answer. Choice A gets the elasticities backwards. Choices B, C and D are wrong because who pays a tax depends on elasticities, not on who sends the money to the government."},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01DVVipuGLKTwwVZcMuXdcgp","name":"submit_solution","input":{"answers":[{"item":"1","choice_index":4,"final_answer":"Producers bear the larger share, because supply is less elastic than demand.","brief_reasoning":"Burden falls more on the less elastic side; supply (0.5) is less elastic than demand (3.0), so producers bear about 86% of the tax.","ambiguous_or_flawed":false}]},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":337,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":568,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":391,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"usage":{"input_tokens":337,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":568,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":391,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"cost":0.009395200000000001}
